      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for jhead",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for jhead fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in jhead:\n\n- CVE-2024-2824: heap-based buffer overflow in function PrintFormatNumber (bsc#1221918)\n- CVE-2025-44906: v3.08 was discovered to contain a heap-use-after-free via the ProcessFile function at jhead.c. (bsc#1243819)\n- CVE-2026-90681: Denial of service via out-of-bounds read in EXIF parsing (bsc#1280205)\n- CVE-2026-90682: heap buffer overflow in in `Get32s` when processing GPS rational values from malformed WebP EXIF chunks (bsc#1280482)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-packagehub-747",
